<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Test on Antomor</title><link>https://antomor.com/tags/test/</link><description>Recent content in Test on Antomor</description><generator>Hugo -- gohugo.io</generator><language>en</language><managingEditor>dev@antomor.com (Antonio Morrone)</managingEditor><webMaster>dev@antomor.com (Antonio Morrone)</webMaster><copyright>© 2026 Antonio Morrone</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 25 Aug 2019 10:48:40 +0200</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://antomor.com/tags/test/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Let's Test</title><link>https://antomor.com/blog/lets-test/</link><pubDate>Sun, 25 Aug 2019 10:48:40 +0200</pubDate><author>dev@antomor.com (Antonio Morrone)</author><guid>https://antomor.com/blog/lets-test/</guid><description>&lt;h2 class="relative group"&gt;Preamble&#10; &lt;div id="preamble" class="anchor"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &#10; &lt;span&#10; class="absolute top-0 w-6 transition-opacity opacity-0 -start-6 not-prose group-hover:opacity-100 select-none"&gt;&#10; &lt;a class="text-primary-300 dark:text-neutral-700 !no-underline" href="#preamble" aria-label="Anchor"&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&#10; &lt;/span&gt;&#10; &#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;This article is not intended to cover the whole &lt;em&gt;testing process&lt;/em&gt; due to its vastness. Having a glance at its &lt;a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_testing" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer"&gt;Wikipedia page&lt;/a&gt; could give an idea of it. I am going to cover only the tip of the iceberg, but it is important to remember that bugs cannot be entirely eliminated from software — instead, they &lt;strong&gt;must&lt;/strong&gt; be discovered as soon as possible.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>